===A7_S2_D2===
Noelle: (You can really feel how strong the waves are from here!) #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Narrator: Your awe is cut short when Zale grabs onto a fish, and immediately bites down on it to knock it unconscious.
Noelle: ?! #portrait:NoelleShocked
Narrator: The Ichthyos join him, laughing gleefully as they enjoy their breakfast…
Hugo: First time? #portrait:Hugo
Noelle: Ah… #portrait:NoelleUm
Hugo: In the same way some predatory creatures may consume meat, so do the Ichthyos. #portrait:Hugo
Hugo: We Krakenfolk prefer to cook our seafood first, though… #portrait:Hugo
Noelle: I… think I’ll pass. #portrait:NoelleSad
Narrator: Hugo barks out a laugh.
Hugo: Suit yourself. #portrait:Hugo
Hugo: We do have some vegetarians on shore. You can find some bread and soups like they serve in the human settlement once you resurface. #portrait:Hugo
Hugo: For now… #portrait:Hugo
Narrator: You hear the Krakenfolk in the fishing boats above call out. They’ve stuck their heads into the water to ask the others to start passing them supplies.
Aditi: We haven’t got all day, y’know!
Zale: Right, right. #portrait:Zale
Hugo: I’ll go help them. Talk to you soon? #portrait:Hugo
Noelle: Yeah… see you. #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: You’re starting to realize that this is the first time you’ve encountered meat.
Narrator: The humans eat eggs and sometimes fish, you’ve heard… but that’s only when they’re brought over as gifts from the ocean.
Noelle: (At least they’re only taking what they need, I guess…?) #portrait:NoelleSad
Narrator: As the day continues, with the Ichthyos and Krakenfolk guiding you further away from shore…
Narrator: You begin to realize a few things.
Noelle: (They can predict the weather and tides for the next week just by sensing it from the water… and monitor how long we have until the floods come in.) #portrait:NoelleShocked
Noelle: (Not to mention that they’re acquainted with so many sea creatures. Despite their playful sides, the Ichthyos are paying close attention to everything around them.) #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Ada: Hey! What’cha doin? #portrait:Ada
Noelle: Trying to figure out how to swim faster. I can tell you guys are going easy on me. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Noelle: …To be honest, this is kind of amazing. I never would’ve imagined that I’d be able to come down underwater for so long. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Ada: Well, that’s just the start! #portrait:Ada
Ada: If you’re up for it, I can show you how to move faster, ‘see’ your surroundings while you’re swimming. #portrait:Ada
Ada: Before you know it, it’s easier than it is to walk! #portrait:Ada
Noelle: I probably look like a duckling, don’t I? #portrait:NoelleUm
Ada: Oh, it’s nothing. All the Krakenfolk were the same. #portrait:Ada
Narrator: Ada leans in conspirationally.
Ada: Some were even afraid of the water! #portrait:Ada
Narrator: As the next days pass, you continue joining the Ichthyos and Krakenfolk in their daily activities. 
Narrator: As you return to the usual diving spot, you realize that Ada’s right.
Narrator: Going underwater now feels as easy as breathing air.
